From: macos15-guest-stack <kirin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] gfx: serve the protocol-version register lock-free (0x1034)

The guest reads 0x1034 as its first matching act, before it has written
anything.  gfx_read answered it from the device lock, so when the drain
worker held that lock the read fell through to the gfx_read_cache, which
had never held the register and returned 0: AppleParavirtGPU matched
against version 0, switched its whole feature set off and never started
(the 2026-09-17 boot stall).

GfxRegs::version becomes the negotiated value's single source and an
Arc<AtomicU32> shared with the registry slot, so device_gfx_read answers
0x1034 from the live atomic exactly like the FIFO-read / fault / interrupt
registers it already serves lock-free.  Negotiation still happens under
the lock in runtime::mmio::gfx_write; the atomic only publishes it.  The
constant EFI capability registers (mode count, mode size, stride align,
display ports, builtin connected) are seeded into the fallback cache at
create and reset instead - they never change, so a lock-busy read gets
the device's own value rather than a cache-miss zero.

Apply on top of 0001 in the reims-vgpu source root:  patch -p1 < this file

